[N 42-43 Stormwind and Aerie Peak]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Stormwind and the search for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar: Brohann Caskbelly sends you to the Pool of Tears in the Swamp of Sorrows, Andromath's supplies go by Darkshire to Nethergarde Keep on the way; then Aerie Peak for Falstad, Gryphon Master Talonaxe and Rhapsody Shindigger, whose Kalimdor Kocktail rides with you to Tanaris and Feralas.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  this chapter wants level 42. The highest required level of its quests is 40 (Vital Supplies and Supplies for Nethergarde); the 42 is the ground: the dragonkin round the Pool of Tears are 41-45 and the Hinterlands mobs on the walk to Rhapsody 41-44. Nothing here has to be killed. Under 42: ride round the packs, come into the Pool's ring from the south, and on the Hinterlands walk keep to the road
[OC]|cffffffffStormwind and Aerie Peak|r  -  you start in Ironforge after chapter 43 with the hearth at Farholde Keep. This chapter binds Stormwind: from the Pool of Tears the hearth (or Astral Recall) takes you straight back to Brohann. Every flight point it uses is known (Stormwind, Darkshire, Nethergarde Keep, Aerie Peak). 7 quests, 12,290 XP and 50s; no quest here has a reward choice
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Delivering Closure (94893, Marshal Ryan's Crest), only if you were given it: it is handed in in Stormwind. Friz Frazzlespark's errands (I Know a Guy 95295, From Port to Port 95219, Shipping and Handling 95296 if taken) ride on untouched
[OC]|cffffcc00Training:|r the level 42 row was bought in Ironforge in chapter 43; Farseer Maret Firetend in Aerie Peak is the fallback if you skipped it. The level 44 row is chapter 48's

